.\n\nThe input archive freezes both complete HIP adaptations, the retained-upstream comparison wrapper, seeded FP16 inputs, provenance and runner. Each host archive retains all outputs, runtime guards, binary and compiler-reported sources/headers. Both hosts pass 48 paired trials (96 launches each) at 1, 3, 64 and 256 rows, Q32/K8 heads, full128 rotation, block512/wave64.\n\nIndependent CPU float64 and Torch FP32 audits compare 79,626,240 values, with zero tolerance failures and zero Torch/adapted/upstream bit differences. The source component check proves full program binding, initialized mutable interfaces and conditional ownership/race lemmas, with 99 audits and nine false Lean controls.\n\nComplete native launch execution, classification of the universal actual trace and source/reference equality are pending; zero native RoPE source certificates are issued. This is not an original-paper production certificate, historical model result or NVIDIA execution/timing result. Model calls are zero. IEEE/error guarantees remain outside the paper formal scope.\n"}